00:01.920 --> 00:03.390
No way!

00:03.390 --> 00:05.310
Captain Tezuka actually lost.

00:05.810 --> 00:08.430
Furthermore, even Fuji-senpai is...{in a pinch.}

00:20.450 --> 00:22.340
That shot went so high up.

00:22.340 --> 00:22.920
I... I can't see the ball.

00:22.910 --> 00:24.870
I... I can't see the ball.

00:34.000 --> 00:35.630
Meteor Drive.

00:42.940 --> 00:44.390
15-0.

00:45.980 --> 00:48.310
T-There's no way to return... {He couldn't have returned that shot.}

00:48.310 --> 00:49.770
such a shot.

00:50.750 --> 00:52.190
30-0.

00:53.870 --> 00:55.110
40-0.

00:55.110 --> 00:56.800
Match point.

00:57.840 --> 00:59.820
Fuji-senpai's going to lose?

00:59.820 --> 01:05.000
Just like that, Seigaku will lose without a fighting chance?

01:07.920 --> 01:09.330
Meteor Drive!

02:35.090 --> 02:36.510
Meteor Drive!

02:44.250 --> 02:45.970
Fuji retreated to the service line.

02:45.970 --> 02:47.230
I see.

02:47.230 --> 02:50.140
He plans to return the shot directly when it lands.

02:51.760 --> 02:53.160
<i>From this position...</i>

02:53.960 --> 02:56.110
<i>I'll be able to see through it completely.</i>

03:01.990 --> 03:02.760
Where?

03:02.760 --> 03:03.910
Where's the ball?

03:09.760 --> 03:11.790
Where are you looking?

03:12.530 --> 03:14.130
The ball's right here.

03:15.060 --> 03:16.750
A-At such a place?

03:18.670 --> 03:20.120
Damn.

03:20.120 --> 03:22.610
He's completely trifling with Fuji. {He's completely trifling with Fuji.}

03:27.060 --> 03:31.290
It's about time I paint you red as well.

03:37.520 --> 03:38.900
He appeared!

03:39.590 --> 03:41.860
D-Devil Akaya.

03:43.840 --> 03:46.110
That's a nice expression, Fuji!{That's a nice mug, Fuji.}

03:46.110 --> 03:49.790
Your nationals ends right here!

03:53.250 --> 03:54.410
Fuji!

03:59.180 --> 04:00.890
A dream, huh?

04:02.910 --> 04:05.140
You should be lying down.

04:09.730 --> 04:11.230
We lost, didn't we?

04:11.230 --> 04:12.060
Both of us.

04:12.890 --> 04:15.020
I'm sorry, Kaidoh.

04:22.570 --> 04:23.640
Don't be. {No, in fact...}

04:23.640 --> 04:25.450
Thank you very much.

04:29.910 --> 04:32.330
We'll leave it to you, Fuji. {Please pull through, Fuji.}

04:35.460 --> 04:36.660
Game, Seigaku.

04:36.660 --> 04:38.290
3-0.

04:38.290 --> 04:39.940
That did it! {That ends it!}

04:39.940 --> 04:41.910
Triple Counter: Hakuryu! {Triple Dragon}

04:41.910 --> 04:44.720
That was a perfect chance, Fuji-senpai.

04:44.720 --> 04:46.620
Obviously! {Naturally}

04:46.620 --> 04:48.080
Right, Echizen?

04:48.080 --> 04:49.390
Y-Yeah.

04:50.640 --> 04:51.470
Next.

04:51.470 --> 04:52.350
Here it comes.

04:52.780 --> 04:54.440
Fifth Counter: Hecatoncheires no Monban. {The gatekeeper Hecatoncheire }

04:54.440 --> 04:56.270
Fifth Counter: Hecatoncheires no Monban. {The gatekeeper Hecatoncheire }

04:56.270 --> 04:58.580
Here comes the fifth counter!

04:58.580 --> 04:59.520
What?

04:59.520 --> 05:00.490
Fifth? {counter}

05:01.220 --> 05:03.710
That was supposed to be the final counter, right?

05:04.720 --> 05:06.600
Rather than finishing them off easily,

05:06.600 --> 05:09.620
he wants his opponents to show a better performance. {sarani ue o mezasou to yu ishi hyoji kai; literally=Rather than finishing it off easy, he is displaying possibilities his superiority.  }

05:10.330 --> 05:11.790
<i>Fuji.</i>

05:11.790 --> 05:12.850
<i>You...</i>

05:17.360 --> 05:18.830
Your ball...

05:18.830 --> 05:20.460
won't pass the net.

05:28.970 --> 05:30.430
I-Impossible!

05:30.430 --> 05:33.560
Niou-senpai's shots won't cross the net!

05:34.910 --> 05:37.480
So this is Hecatoncheires no Monban.

05:39.730 --> 05:40.980
Game, Seigaku.

05:40.980 --> 05:42.730
4-0.

05:42.730 --> 05:43.930
He did it!

05:43.930 --> 05:45.650
Four games in a row!

05:45.650 --> 05:48.220
Despite losing the last two matches...

05:48.220 --> 05:49.020
Yes.

05:49.020 --> 05:51.580
If this continues, we'll catch up in no time.

05:52.390 --> 05:53.880
Hey, Niou.

05:53.880 --> 05:55.910
You played around a bit too much. {You lpayed around a little too much}

05:55.910 --> 05:58.230
That was merely data collection.

05:58.230 --> 06:00.820
Could you please shut up for a little longer?

06:03.950 --> 06:05.000
That guy...

06:05.500 --> 06:06.820
Just let it go.

06:06.820 --> 06:09.320
We need to be wary of Fuji after all. {Fuji is one to watch out for after all.}

06:09.980 --> 06:13.000
Even he will need to make preparations for that.

06:14.140 --> 06:15.680
What is he plotting?

06:16.910 --> 06:19.530
Even to the genius Fuji Shusuke,

06:19.530 --> 06:21.670
he's definitely an unbeatable opponent now.

06:21.670 --> 06:22.650
Apparently.

06:22.650 --> 06:25.320
Unbeatable opponent?

06:25.320 --> 06:27.610
It's about time it shows up.

06:36.340 --> 06:38.910
T-This can't be...{This is not possible...}

06:43.330 --> 06:45.100
T-That is...

06:45.100 --> 06:46.000
That can't be right. {Unbelievable!}

06:47.340 --> 06:48.130
<i>A-Am I seeing a dream? {Am I dreaming?}</i>

06:48.130 --> 06:49.970
<i>A-Am I seeing a dream?</i>

06:58.540 --> 06:59.980
Tezuka.

07:03.860 --> 07:05.260
Tezuka, huh? {So, he picked Tazuka.}

07:06.600 --> 07:08.700
This is just the beginning...

07:08.700 --> 07:11.320
of the godliness of his illusions. {I used this 信心 shinjin= godliness or did he say shinji 【芯地 ・ 心地】= foundation? Please confirm.}

07:14.740 --> 07:16.860
Muga no Kyouchi!? {State of Self Actualization}

07:16.860 --> 07:18.410
No.

07:18.410 --> 07:21.330
That's Hyakuren Jitoku no Kiwami. { That's the 'Pinnacle of hard work}

07:23.560 --> 07:26.250
W-What!? Hyakuren Jitoku?

07:26.250 --> 07:28.300
Still, even though it's Fuji-senpai...

07:28.300 --> 07:30.200
This is disastrous.

07:33.430 --> 07:34.640
Come, Fuji!

07:41.110 --> 07:42.520
0-15.

07:43.660 --> 07:45.110
A double return!

07:45.110 --> 07:47.190
A no-touch return ace!

07:54.460 --> 07:55.780
0-30.

07:59.700 --> 08:01.180
In every single way,

08:01.180 --> 08:02.570
he's exactly like Tezuka.

08:02.570 --> 08:05.070
Even though we've seen imitations of people's mannerisms before,

08:05.070 --> 08:06.850
actually becoming the person itself...

08:06.850 --> 08:08.630
That has never happened before, right?

08:09.910 --> 08:13.090
What a fearful imposter of the court. {petenshi, can also be substituted with swindler / crook}

08:14.830 --> 08:16.300
Your illusion...

08:16.300 --> 08:19.060
seems more than just a bluff.

08:22.800 --> 08:26.900
<i>I never thought that I would be fighting against you like this,</i>

08:27.280 --> 08:28.190
<i>Tezuka.</i>

08:39.200 --> 08:40.670
Triple Counter: Hakuryu.

08:40.670 --> 08:41.750
Triple Counter: Hakuryu.

08:46.630 --> 08:48.420
Even before it bounces, he...

08:49.630 --> 08:51.190
That would end it... for Fuji!

08:51.190 --> 08:52.050
That would end it... for Fuji!

08:55.450 --> 08:56.690
<i>Triple Counter: Kirin Otoshi. {Kirin Drop}</i>

08:56.690 --> 08:57.970
<i>Triple Counter: Kirin Otoshi. {Kirin Drop}</i>

08:59.290 --> 09:00.930
T-The ball is...{going into the...}{additional unsaid words for clarity}

09:00.930 --> 09:02.350
Tezuka Zone.

09:05.730 --> 09:07.220
That stance is...

09:07.220 --> 09:08.200
I see.

09:08.200 --> 09:10.470
He purposely made him return that shot with a top spin.

09:10.470 --> 09:12.150
Triple Counter: Houou Gaeshi.

09:12.150 --> 09:14.150
Triple Counter: Houou Gaeshi. {Phoenix Return}

09:19.070 --> 09:20.340
0-40.

09:21.680 --> 09:24.220
He returned the triple counters,

09:24.220 --> 09:27.180
then finished the game off with the Zero Shiki Drop Shot. {Zero Direction Drop Shot}

09:27.180 --> 09:28.960
This is just like...

09:28.960 --> 09:32.880
a match between the real Captain Tezuka and Fuji-senpai, isn't it?

09:39.180 --> 09:44.750
With his illusions, he can even become Sanada or me.

09:44.750 --> 09:45.800
What did you say?

09:47.300 --> 09:48.850
That's what he said.

09:55.210 --> 09:55.650
Out!

09:56.500 --> 09:58.440
Game, Rikkaidai Fuzoku.

09:58.440 --> 10:00.030
1-4.

10:00.030 --> 10:01.760
You can't be serious.

10:01.760 --> 10:04.040
Even the Tezuka Phantom...{Imitating even the Tzuka Phantom...}

10:07.120 --> 10:08.190
In a sense, {In a sense,}

10:08.190 --> 10:11.420
Niou is the most troublesome opponent in Rikkai. {substitue for troublesome= difficult/ toughest}{alternatively: Niou is possibly the toughest opponent in Rikkaidai.} {adding possibly or probably here->deleting next sentence}

10:11.420 --> 10:12.550
Possibly.

10:16.830 --> 10:19.350
The tides are completely turning in Rikkai's favor.

10:19.350 --> 10:22.870
This might end miserably for Seigaku. {惨憺santan= miserable, pitiful, tragic}{Alternatively: Seigaku, this might even end miserably for them.}

10:22.870 --> 10:28.350
Niou's illusion is different from those who mimic a superior they admire. {it's a different league from those who mimics a superior.}

10:28.350 --> 10:31.690
It's impossible unless you have the ability to emulate the actual person.

10:31.690 --> 10:34.610
It doesn't matter if it's the genuine article or a counterfeit.

10:34.610 --> 10:37.420
Apart from that, Fuji regards Tezuka as... {Apart from that, Fuji regards Tezuka as...}

10:38.130 --> 10:39.200
I see.

10:39.200 --> 10:40.360
That's well thought out. {That's well thought out.}

10:40.850 --> 10:42.270
The truth is,

10:42.270 --> 10:47.340
such seemingly unmatched gems of Seigaku appearing here is beyond my imagination.

10:59.720 --> 11:01.550
Even at a time like this, I'm wondering...

11:01.930 --> 11:03.630
What's the matter, Horio-kun?

11:03.630 --> 11:08.790
Who is actually stronger between Captain Tezuka and Fuji-senpai?

11:09.450 --> 11:12.020
When they played in a match before the national tournament,

11:12.020 --> 11:13.810
Captain Tezuka won.

11:13.810 --> 11:15.700
So he must be stronger after all.

11:16.200 --> 11:17.950
I wouldn't decide on that yet.

11:18.740 --> 11:21.570
It's true that Tezuka won back then,

11:21.570 --> 11:24.660
but Fuji has been improving gradually during this tournament.

11:24.660 --> 11:27.990
We can't really tell at this point in time.

11:29.700 --> 11:34.050
Did Captain Tezuka and Fuji-senpai ever play against each other besides that match?

11:34.050 --> 11:36.690
Now that you mention it, even in our ranking matches,

11:36.690 --> 11:39.590
I don't recall them ever matching up against each other.

11:39.590 --> 11:42.160
So that recent match was the only time then?

11:42.160 --> 11:43.100
No.

11:43.100 --> 11:45.390
There was one a long time ago. {There was once, a long time ago.}

11:46.940 --> 11:47.850
The result? {Who won?}

11:49.230 --> 11:51.770
I don't know the details either.

11:56.390 --> 11:57.440
<i>It's strange.</i>

11:58.460 --> 12:00.150
<i>Ever since we were freshmen,</i>

12:00.150 --> 12:02.900
<i>I've seen your face almost every day. {I see you almost everyday since we were freshmen.}</i>

12:02.900 --> 12:05.990
<i>But to see you across the net like this...</i>

12:05.120 --> 12:08.450
<i>It feels nostalgic.</i>

12:18.310 --> 12:19.810
<i>Ever since that day,</i>

12:19.810 --> 12:23.050
<i>I've desperately looked forward to meeting you in a competition. {I had waited in anticipation to meeting you in a competition.}</i>

12:23.540 --> 12:26.220
<i>So much that you wouldn't even imagine it.</i>

12:32.200 --> 12:34.390
From what I heard two years ago,

12:34.390 --> 12:36.810
Fuji won 6-0.

12:37.200 --> 12:39.230
Tezuka was completely beaten. {Tezuka was copletely defeated.}

12:41.740 --> 12:43.630
What are you babbling about over there!?

12:43.630 --> 12:45.360
Keep up the cheers for the team.{How about cheering for the team?}

12:45.360 --> 12:46.780
Y-Yes!

12:47.630 --> 12:49.980
For now, let's just concentrate on Fuji's match.

12:49.980 --> 12:51.000
Good grief.

12:58.750 --> 13:01.050
It's a double return with Hyakuren Jitoku.

13:06.070 --> 13:08.250
This time it's Kagerou Zutsumi. {Dragonfly Illusion}

13:11.090 --> 13:12.640
But...

13:13.180 --> 13:14.970
Game, Rikkaidai Fuzoku.

13:14.970 --> 13:17.020
4-4.

13:17.020 --> 13:19.440
He has finally caught up.

13:20.280 --> 13:22.210
Catching up to that four-game lead... {orig: He did it with a four game lead.}{TLC: please check the line for accuracy.}

13:22.210 --> 13:24.400
He has surely made his point clear to them. {achiibu 【アチーブ】-achieve}{He's displaying quite an achievement there.}

13:24.400 --> 13:25.780
That Fuji...

13:25.780 --> 13:27.390
What will he do now?

13:27.390 --> 13:31.410
He seems focused, but he is actually distracted.

13:31.410 --> 13:33.080
That's how it feels to me anyway.

13:41.600 --> 13:42.920
<i>That day,</i>

13:43.710 --> 13:47.800
<i>due to your injuries, you lost to me.  {I heard 危急で不肖侭 kikyuu de o fushou mama- with only emergency treatments to your condition of misfortune... But I used injuries here. Easier to understand?}</i>

13:48.580 --> 13:51.030
<i>We were going to have a rematch someday...</i>

13:51.030 --> 13:52.260
<i>when your arm had healed completely. {Line 215-216, can also be structured as: We were goimg to have a return match someday, when your hand heals completely.}</i>

13:52.940 --> 13:55.230
<i>That was our promise, wasn't it? {We made such a promise, didn't we? }</i>

13:56.350 --> 13:57.830
<i>It has been two years since then.</i>

13:57.830 --> 14:00.190
<i>You fulfilled your promise to me. {You fulfilled your part of the promise to me.}</i>

14:03.020 --> 14:04.970
<i>I was thoroughly defeated.</i>

14:04.970 --> 14:07.150
<i>As I thought, you are really strong. {You are truly strong after all.}</i>

14:07.150 --> 14:10.470
<i>I've come to realize my own weakness.</i>

14:20.840 --> 14:22.700
Game, Rikkaidai Fuzoku.

14:22.700 --> 14:24.300
5-4.

14:24.300 --> 14:26.500
He broke through the Hecatoncheires no Monban...

14:26.500 --> 14:28.200
and turned the game around.

14:28.200 --> 14:31.970
If this keeps up, all the counters will be defeated. {With this, all the counters will be destroyed. }

14:32.570 --> 14:38.220
While Fuji is called a genius, 
he still has a wall that he can't overcome.

14:38.220 --> 14:41.950
If there was anything that could stop the ever evolving Fuji,

14:41.950 --> 14:43.650
it could only be Tezuka.

14:43.650 --> 14:47.340
In other words, if Fuji doesn't overcome Tezuka now,

14:47.340 --> 14:49.570
it will be impossible for Seigaku to win.

14:50.050 --> 14:52.590
It's finally match game for Rikkaidai.

14:52.590 --> 14:54.620
This is bad. There's nothing left after this.

14:54.620 --> 14:58.540
He could finish this game easily with just four more Zero Shiki Serves.{He only has to finish this last game with 4 more Zero Shiki serves.}

14:59.430 --> 15:00.710
Six shots.

15:02.520 --> 15:04.500
Saikikanpatsu no Kiwami!{Pinnacle of Great Wisdom}

15:04.500 --> 15:07.550
He's going for the absolute prediction here? {I heard this yukoku 【諭告】= admonition. Please confirm if this is a Pot play that's missed out on the list. Zettai yukoku }

15:07.550 --> 15:10.590
He wants to finish with a perfect clincher here. {alternatively substitute finish with end}

15:11.390 --> 15:12.510
Fuji...

15:16.910 --> 15:19.310
Oh, God!

15:27.030 --> 15:28.080
H-How could he...?

15:28.080 --> 15:29.900
H-How could he...?

15:31.820 --> 15:33.370
What happened?

15:33.370 --> 15:36.240
He's exceeded the six shots predicted by the absolute prediction. {zettai yukoku}

15:36.670 --> 15:37.700
Hey, look!

15:40.970 --> 15:42.050
Fuji-senpai...

15:42.050 --> 15:43.330
has closed both of his eyes.

15:43.920 --> 15:45.790
Closed eyes.

15:45.790 --> 15:48.760
He's breaking through Saikikanpatsu with his eyes closed. {Saikikanpatsu no Kiwami}

15:51.920 --> 15:53.970
Smashing with movements from his entire body.

15:53.970 --> 15:56.430
Plainly returning all balls in a straightforward manner. {alternatively, replace forward manner with dorectly}

15:57.140 --> 16:02.980
With that, Saikikanpatsu's absolute prediction is rendered ineffective. {TLC: original line is not clear. please confirm}

16:03.970 --> 16:05.650
Not bad at all. {Not bad at all.}

16:12.750 --> 16:13.930
Game, Seigaku.

16:13.930 --> 16:15.780
5-5.

16:22.910 --> 16:23.910
That guy...

16:23.910 --> 16:27.380
could actually aim for a cord ball with both eyes closed?

16:27.380 --> 16:30.880
This is what it means to be called a genius, huh?

16:30.880 --> 16:36.340
Fuji's defeat in the semifinals has brought him to new heights.

16:41.450 --> 16:42.570
Game, Seigaku.

16:42.570 --> 16:44.190
6-5.

16:44.190 --> 16:46.050
All right!

16:46.050 --> 16:47.650
He made a close comeback!

16:47.650 --> 16:48.560
Amazing!

16:48.560 --> 16:50.560
You're amazing, Fuji-senpai.

16:50.560 --> 16:52.570
Don't cry, Horio-kun.

16:52.570 --> 16:53.590
<b>Fuji! Fuji! Fuji!</b>

16:53.590 --> 16:54.640
<b>Fuji! Fuji! Fuji!</b>

16:54.640 --> 16:55.660
<b>Fuji! Fuji! Fuji!</b>

16:55.660 --> 16:56.610
<b>Fuji! Fuji! Fuji!</b>

16:56.610 --> 16:57.590
<b>Fuji! Fuji! Fuji!</b>

16:57.590 --> 16:58.700
<b>Fuji! Fuji! Fuji!</b>

16:58.280 --> 16:59.450
Hey, hey!

17:01.450 --> 17:05.160
Even Tezuka Kunimitsu is unexpectedly useless.

17:05.160 --> 17:10.100
More accurately, your illusion isn't perfect, is it?

17:10.100 --> 17:10.880
What?

17:11.420 --> 17:14.070
In your service game earlier,

17:14.070 --> 17:16.820
I was deceived by Saikikanpatsu. {alternatively: I was misled by Saikikanpatsu}

17:16.820 --> 17:20.440
You could've easily won with just four Zero Shiki Serves.

17:20.440 --> 17:21.850
But you didn't hit them.

17:22.490 --> 17:24.520
No, you couldn't hit them.

17:25.740 --> 17:28.440
Illusion is just illusion after all.

17:29.100 --> 17:33.580
From the start, however, I was able to reminisce because of that.{HE said motomo- from the start / originally, but do consider changing this to 'But',However instead.}{However, its was due to that I was able to reminisce.}

17:34.170 --> 17:38.240
And then regain my genuine feelings toward tennis.

17:39.950 --> 17:41.740
I can only say this.

17:42.440 --> 17:45.710
You do not hold a candle to Tezuka at all.

17:47.620 --> 17:49.680
What's with Fuji?

17:49.680 --> 17:53.580
Hasn't he reached his limits with all his counters destroyed?

17:54.410 --> 17:58.220
He must have been thinking of something else while playing.

17:58.220 --> 18:01.600
As expected, Fuji wasn't about to be deceived by an imposter.

18:01.600 --> 18:03.380
Well, that's beside the point. {Well, it's not about that.}

18:03.380 --> 18:06.540
On the contrary, he went along for the ride completely.

18:08.820 --> 18:11.400
As I thought, his opponent was above him.

18:15.910 --> 18:17.340
How about this?

18:19.640 --> 18:20.770
That is...

18:20.770 --> 18:23.050
Shiraishi from Shitenhouji.

18:23.050 --> 18:26.200
The one who defeated Fuji in the semifinals; the Bible.

18:27.680 --> 18:31.210
There are other opponents that you're weak against.

18:31.620 --> 18:35.460
Sorry, but I never lose twice to the same opponent.

18:36.140 --> 18:37.300
Here it comes.

18:37.300 --> 18:38.820
Sixth Counter: Hoshi Hanabi. {Star Fireworks}{TL Note: Hoshi Hanabi means "Star Fireworks."}

18:38.820 --> 18:40.130
Sixth Counter: Hoshi Hanabi.

18:40.160 --> 18:41.590
Hoshi Hanabi!?

18:42.910 --> 18:45.010
It's the sixth counter!

18:45.010 --> 18:46.980
Is he still evolving?

18:46.980 --> 18:47.930
Fuji-senpai!

18:51.320 --> 18:54.710
I've already returned all of your prided counters.

18:54.710 --> 18:56.110
You shouldn't lie. You shouldn't...

18:56.110 --> 18:57.360
You shouldn't lie. You shouldn't...

19:01.990 --> 19:04.190
He's now bluffing after his tricks? {TLC: line is not clear as it is}

19:04.190 --> 19:06.160
Fuji has some balls too.

19:13.100 --> 19:15.960
Well then, I shall make you lose to the same opponent twice.

19:18.130 --> 19:22.090
<i>If you really do have a sixth counter, then prove it!</i>

19:25.470 --> 19:27.490
There's no need to worry anymore.

19:28.700 --> 19:31.890
Fuji isn't the type who will lose twice to the same opponent.

19:33.720 --> 19:36.270
So <i>that</i> has been completed as well?

19:45.400 --> 19:48.330
W-What happened?

19:48.330 --> 19:50.430
A-Amazing.

19:50.430 --> 19:52.540
Did you see that?

19:53.720 --> 19:56.460
Even in broad daylight, there were stars.

19:58.330 --> 20:01.320
N-No matter what I do,

20:01.320 --> 20:03.930
there's no way I can return that.

20:05.640 --> 20:07.570
<b>Game and match, Seigaku.</b>

20:07.570 --> 20:09.850
<b>7-5.</b>

20:15.860 --> 20:17.570
I lost! I lost!

20:17.570 --> 20:21.190
Next time, though, I'll break your spirit.

20:23.570 --> 20:25.160
I look forward to that.

20:33.030 --> 20:38.710
After this tournament, would you have a rematch with me again?

20:41.440 --> 20:42.880
My sentiments exactly.  {As I've desired.}

22:11.270 --> 22:14.390
Seigaku seems to be in dispute with their freshman,

22:14.390 --> 22:15.350
but that doesn't matter now.

22:15.840 --> 22:17.130
Next will be me and...

22:17.130 --> 22:18.630
Nezumihana Beat. {nezumihanabi 【鼠花火】=pinwheel, he said bito=beat}

22:18.630 --> 22:20.750
That's my partner Jackal.

22:20.750 --> 22:23.750
We'll show you the true abilities of the nation's number one doubles team.

22:23.750 --> 22:25.400
Nezumihana Beat.

22:25.400 --> 22:26.690
Hey, Oishi and Kikumaru.

22:26.690 --> 22:29.160
This isn't the time to worry about your freshman.

22:29.160 --> 22:31.030
Nezumihana Beat!

22:31.030 --> 22:33.220
Next time: Our Hearts as One. {TL Check: please verify the translation of this line; original line is: With Hearts as One.}

22:33.220 --> 22:35.370
We'll crown the final match with our victory.

22:35.780 --> 22:36.830
It's not the final match.

22:36.830 --> 22:37.830
What do you mean?

22:37.830 --> 22:39.300
Nezumihana Beat!

22:39.300 --> 22:40.330
Jackal!
